## Why This Is Asked
Gauges candidate ability to architect a small, realistic feature with performance thoughts and React hooks.

## Key Concepts
- In-memory indexing for fast, offline search
- Debounce input and memoize results
- Component memoization to avoid re-renders

## Code Example
```javascript
const EMOJIS = [
  {char:'😀', name:'grinning'},
  {char:'🎉', name:'party'},
  {char:'🚀', name:'rocket'}
];

function useEmojiSearch(query){
  const [q, setQ] = React.useState(query);
  const [debounced, setDebounced] = React.useState(query);
  React.useEffect(() => {
    const t = setTimeout(() => setDebounced(q), 150);
    return () => clearTimeout(t);
  }, [q]);
  const results = React.useMemo(
    () => EMOJIS.filter(e => e.name.toLowerCase().includes(debounced.toLowerCase())),
    [debounced]
  );
  return { query: q, setQuery: setQ, results };
}
```

```javascript
function EmojiPicker(){
  const { query, setQuery, results } = useEmojiSearch('');
  return (
    <>
      <TextInput value={query} onChangeText={setQuery} placeholder="Search emoji" />
      <FlatList
        data={results}
        horizontal
        keyExtractor={e => e.name}
        renderItem={({ item }) => (
          <Text accessibilityLabel={item.name}>{item.char}</Text>
        )}
      />
    </>
  );
}
```

